{"id":"38b3d2937e3a28aa710b86d83b71db18b1980ba7","axis":"silent","repo":"strapi/strapi","sha":"38b3d2937e3a28aa710b86d83b71db18b1980ba7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/docs/packages/core/admin/permissions/01-how-they-work.md","lines":["@@ -150,3 +150,21 @@ The permissions are modified in the admin panel (on the [edit page](http://local"," | **conditions**       | List of the conditions that will be ran against an entry to determine whether the action on this entry is permitted or not | array  | -        | `['admin::is-creator']`                                       |"," "," A permission contains all needed information for the backend and the frontend to prevent users to perform non-permitted action.","+","+### Permission ceiling","+","+A user can only hand on permissions they hold themselves. The rules live in `server/src/domain/permission/ceiling.ts`.","+","+The engine registers each stored permission as its own rule (`title@en` plus `body@fr` does not give `title@fr`), and the ceiling does the same. A requested permission is split into atoms (one per field, locale and condition combination). It is within the ceiling when each atom is covered by a single held permission with the same `action` and `subject`. Different atoms can be covered by different held permissions. A held permission covers a value if it does not restrict that property or lists the value (`seo` covers `seo.title`), and covers a condition if it is unconditional or lists it. Omitting a restricted property, sending `null` or dropping conditions is rejected.","+","+Held permissions are read as the engine enforces them:","+","+- `fields: []` grants nothing. On a localized subject, a missing `locales` means `locales: []`, even for a super admin's token.","+- A permission with action parameters does not hold the plain action, nor does one whose conditions are all unknown. It is registered as `<action>?<parameters>`, so only held permissions with the same action, subject and parameters cover it (`isParameterizedPermissionWithinCeiling`), using the same atom rule.","+- Unions on one dimension are fine (`title` and `body` held separately allow `[title, body]`); mixing dimensions is not.","+","+Where it applies:","+","+- **Roles**: `PUT /admin/roles/:id/permissions` returns 403 with the offending permissions in `error.details.permissions`. Super admins are exempt. An admin-token request is checked against the token's permissions and, unless the owner is a super admin, the owner's too (`findRequesterCeilings` in `server/src/services/permission/ceiling-requester.ts`). Permissions the role already carries are not checked, whatever their array order, and neither is a narrowing of one of the role's rows (every atom covered by one existing row, so fewer fields, locales or conditions pass). Recombining two rows, or dropping a row's last condition, is checked. Parameterized requests are never a narrowing. Creating or duplicating a role uses the same endpoint, so the duplicate page first drops source permissions outside the user's ceiling.","+- **Admin tokens**: `enforceAdminPermissionsCeiling` in `server/src/services/api-token.ts` rejects (400) permissions the owner does not cover and takes conditions from the owner, not the request. Super-admin owners are unlimited. An admin-token request is limited by the same two ceilings as a role update, and can only read the key of, or regenerate, its own token. Token permissions are re-clamped at startup and whenever the owner's roles change (`reconcileTokenPermissionsToUserCeiling`): uncovered permissions are deleted and conditions follow the owner, with a log warning each time. Parameterized token permissions are reconciled only against the owner's permissions with the same action, subject and parameters (`reconcileParameterizedTokenPermissions`), so they are deleted once the owner loses that exact grant.","+- **Role editor**: `admin/src/pages/Settings/pages/Roles/utils/createPermissionChecker.ts` mirrors the rule and disables values and conditions that cannot be added to what is already ticked. A value is tickable only if the resulting row stays within the editor's permissions, or (edit page only) within what the role already stores. A bulk tick picks one held permission and never mixes fields held under different conditions. A component checkbox is enabled when any field under it can be granted, since roles store a component's fields, not its path."],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/admin/admin/src/pages/Settings/pages/AdminTokens/EditView/components/AdminPermissions.tsx","lines":["@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@ export const AdminPermissions = React.forwardRef<PermissionsAPI, AdminPermission","         layout={layout}","         permissions={initialAdminPermissions}","         userPermissions={effectivePermissions}","+        inheritConditions","         isFormDisabled={disabled}","       />","     );"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/admin/admin/src/pages/Settings/pages/Roles/CreatePage.tsx","lines":["@@ -19,9 +19,11 @@ import { useNavigate, useParams } from 'react-router-dom';"," import { styled } from 'styled-components';"," import * as yup from 'yup';"," ","+import { SUPER_ADMIN_CODE } from '../../../../../../shared/utils/super-admin';"," import { Layouts } from '../../../../components/Layouts/Layout';"," import { Page } from '../../../../components/PageHelpers';"," import { useTypedSelector } from '../../../../core/store/hooks';","+import { useAuth } from '../../../../features/Auth';"," import { BackButton } from '../../../../features/BackButton';"," import { useNotification } from '../../../../features/Notifications';"," import { useTracking } from '../../../../features/Tracking';","@@ -36,6 +38,8 @@ import { isBaseQueryError } from '../../../../utils/baseQuery';"," import { translatedErrors } from '../../../../utils/translatedErrors';"," "," import { Permissions, PermissionsAPI } from './components/Permissions';","+impor